  <Section id="owner" title="High risk, the owner in the loop: #189">
    <Fragment slot="note"><a href={issue(189)}>Issue #189</a>, <a href={pull(194)}>PR #194</a>, 27 October 2026.</Fragment>
    <p class="lede">The feature that introduced the risk level. The owner sharpened its scope in a comment, and caught a defect before the merge.</p>
    <ul class="rules">
      <li><b>A comment as a decision.</b> After the first run, <a href={comment(189, "6443105170")}>the owner's comment</a> set two rules from experience with another project: an escalation reads only changed or removed lines of existing files, and a feature already in progress is not refused.</li>
      <li><b>A resumed session.</b> The owner resumed the implementer by hand, which the run record notes as an intervention. The record also shows the comment passed on to the resumed implementer and to each later review.</li>
      <li><b>A correction before the merge.</b> The owner found that a failed listing of the changed files fell back to the default level. The fix makes it high, with a test that fails against the earlier commit and passes with the fix, as the completion record in the pull request states.</li>
      <li><b>Three rounds, no findings.</b> Review by <code>codex gpt-6-luna</code>, ten of ten criteria met; full verifications of 556, 575 and 572 seconds.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Source files changed by <a href={pull(194)}>PR #194</a>: {changed[194].map((path, i) => (<>{i > 0 && ", "}<a href={repoFile(path)}><code>{path}</code></a></>))}.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="repair" title="High risk, a fix that did not hold: #193">
    <Fragment slot="note"><a href={issue(193)}>Issue #193</a>, <a href={pull(199)}>PR #199</a>, 27 October 2026.</Fragment>
    <p>The feature that made budget checks measurements. In round 1 the reviewer found that a failing timeout utility was reported as an exceeded budget (major) and that a budget's output was cut short (minor); the triage decided to fix both. In round 2 the reviewer raised the major finding again, as “Unresolved M1”: the fix now treated exit status 128 as a failure of the call, though a measurement can return it. A second fix round resolved it, and rounds 3 and 4 passed. Each round's report and triage is <a href={issue(193)}>on the Issue</a>.</p>
    <p>Source files changed by <a href={pull(199)}>PR #199</a>: {changed[199].map((path, i) => (<>{i > 0 && ", "}<a href={repoFile(path)}><code>{path}</code></a></>))}.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="short" title="High risk, the short path: #204 and #16">
