  <Section id="medium" title="Medium risk: #241">
    <Fragment slot="note"><a href={issue(241)}>Issue #241</a>, <a href={pull(249)}>PR #249</a>. One unattended run of <code>run-feature.sh</code>, 30 October 2026.</Fragment>
    <p class="lede">The feature that wrote the first Features, Examples and About pages of this site. It changed website pages only, and it is followed here with the same records as #217.</p>

    <h3>Requirements</h3>
    <p>The Issue asks for the three pages from real repository evidence, with six acceptance criteria; the first reads “Every statement links to or matches its source; no invented figure or testimonial”, and the Examples criterion asks for examples linked to their Issues, pull requests and source files.</p>

    <h3>Risk level and agents</h3>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>risk</dt><dd><span class="lvl medium">medium</span>: the four changed files, three pages and the style sheet, are named by no class of <code>risk.conf</code>, so each gets the default. No escalation applied, the reviewer classified the impact on the architecture as minor, and the triage was full, the default.</dd>
      <dt>implementer</dt><dd><code>claude opus</code>, the plain line <code>implementer</code></dd>
      <dt>fixes</dt><dd><code>claude opus</code>, the plain line <code>triage-implementer</code>; at high, as in #217, <code>claude fable</code></dd>
      <dt>review</dt><dd><code>codex gpt-6-luna</code>, read-only</dd>
      <dt>triage</dt><dd><code>claude sonnet</code>, read-only</dd>
    </dl>

    <h3>Independent review and triage</h3>
    <Table>
      <caption>Rounds 1 and 3 reviewed the complete feature, round 2 only the fix. The triage of round 1 is published on the Issue, marked as approved by an unattended run.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col" class="num">round</th><th scope="col">reviewed</th><th scope="col">verdict</th><th scope="col">finding</th><th scope="col">decision</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {mediumRounds.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="num">{row.link ? <a href={row.link}>{row.round}</a> : row.round}</th>
            <td data-col="reviewed">{row.kind}</td>
            <td data-col="verdict" class="k">{row.verdict}</td>
            <td data-col="finding" class:list={{ off: row.finding === "–" }}>{row.finding}</td>
            <td data-col="decision" class:list={["k", { off: row.decision === "–" }]}>{row.decision}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </Table>
    <p>A medium feature gets the same review as a high one under the shipped policy, and round 1 shows why: the pages linked the source files of only one example, which the Issue asked for every example. A major finding is always fixed; the fix added the source files of the other four, the same lists this page shows under <a href="#features">High risk, more runs</a>.</p>

    <h3>Verification evidence</h3>
    <p>The full verification ran twice, after the implementation and after the fix: 14 and 15 seconds, of which 13 were the check of this site. The workflow's own self-tests in <a href={repoFile("scripts/verify-workflow.conf")}><code>verify-workflow.conf</code></a> run only when a workflow file changes. #217 changed several, so its verifications of 1046 to 1118 seconds included that suite, which the file's header records at 915 seconds when its budget was set; #241 changed none. Five more times a step reused the recorded pass.</p>

    <h3>The run</h3>
    <figure class="plain">
      <svg class="lines" viewBox="0 0 1100 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="run-241-t" aria-describedby="run-241-words">
        <title id="run-241-t">The run of #241: implementation, round 1 and its fix, rounds 2 and 3, commit and pull request, and the merge by the owner.</title>
        <path class="l2" d="M70 60 H1030"/>
        <circle class="dot" cx="70" cy="60" r="10"/><text class="st" x="70" y="97" text-anchor="middle">Implement</text><text class="sub k" x="70" y="117" text-anchor="middle">19:27</text>
