  <Section id="absent" title="What is not shown">
    <Fragment slot="note"><a href={repoFile(".agents/policies/risk.conf")}><code>risk.conf</code></a> of this repository; <a href={issue(170)}>Issue #170</a>.</Fragment>
    <ul class="rules">
      <li><b>A low-risk run.</b> A low level exists only under <code>profile: light</code>, or with a <code>low:</code> class in <code>risk.conf</code>. This repository has neither, so none of its features was low, and this page does not invent one. Under the light profile a low feature may be committed without a review; the commit and the pull request say so, and the merge then needs your approval.</li>
      <li><b>Onboarding an existing repository.</b> Codeyard starts new projects from the template with <code>gh repo create --template</code>. Bringing an existing repository into the workflow is <a href={issue(170)}>planned in #170</a> and not built, so there is no run of it to show.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

